# Root .gitignore.
#
# The three Python subprojects keep their own (PythonWorker/, CarDetection/,
# RoadDamage/); this file covers the repo root and the Xcode project.

# Claude-written markdown — kept local, not shared.
#
# Note for whoever clones this next: the repo's working rules, its ADR record and
# its what's-real-vs-mock status all live in these files, so a fresh clone gets
# none of that context. The architecture reasoning they carry (ADR-015/016: why
# road damage ships boxes not segmentation, why severity is computed only in
# Python, why there are three incompatible venvs) is not recoverable from the
# diff. Ask the repo owner for a copy rather than reconstructing it.
CLAUDE.md
JOURNAL.md
PROGRESS.md
ROAD_DAMAGE_BRIEF.md
.claude
.DS_Store

# Per-user Xcode state: window layout, scroll positions, breakpoints, which
# scheme this particular Mac last selected. Xcode rewrites it constantly, so
# tracked it shows up as a change on every single open and conflicts between
# collaborators for no reason — three people's copies (biru, davindjayadi,
# ignatiusiba) had accumulated in here before this rule existed.
#
# Only `xcuserdata/` is per-user. `xcshareddata/` is NOT ignored on purpose:
# shared schemes live there and are meant to be committed, which is what lets
# a fresh clone build "JalanKita Mac" / "JalanKita iOS" without hand-creating
# a scheme first.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate

# SPM local build products (generated by `xcodebuild ... build`, e.g. when verifying
# a change from the CLI instead of Xcode's own DerivedData) -- regenerable, not source.
build/